  "content": {
    "text": "4 days ago\nMeta shares drop after company reportedly weighs raising billions in equity\nFacebook parent Meta Platforms is reportedly weighing raising equity in the wake of Google parent Alphabet’s massive stock offering to fund its artificial-intelligence infrastructure expansion.\nThe Financial Times reported Friday afternoon that Meta was considering raising tens of billions in dollars in new stock to help fund its own AI ambitions. Bloomberg News on Friday noted that the Financial Times report cited people familiar with discussion. Bloomberg also cited a Meta spokesperson who described the report as “pure speculation.”\nShares of Meta were down almost 6% in late afternoon trading, according to FactSet data, at last check.",
